WEBVTT

00:12:29.234 --> 00:12:31.245
it's things like, physical attractiveness,

00:12:31.269 --> 00:12:33.567
height, eye contact,
how straight your teeth are,

00:12:33.591 --> 00:12:36.043
what your voice sounds like,
your gender, your race.

00:12:36.067 --> 00:12:37.265
There is very little

00:12:37.289 --> 00:12:39.321
that's actually measuring someone's skill,

00:12:39.345 --> 00:12:41.361
or even their ability to relate to people.

00:12:41.385 --> 00:12:43.091
AG: Biases are especially insidious

00:12:43.115 --> 00:12:45.424
because they're usually
invisible to interviewers

00:12:45.448 --> 00:12:47.726
who don't notice
all the little snap judgments

00:12:47.750 --> 00:12:48.916
their brains are making.

00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:52.455
Economists find that candidates
with names like Alison and Matthew

00:12:52.479 --> 00:12:56.031
get 50 percent more callbacks
than Lakisha and Jamal,

00:12:56.055 --> 00:12:58.418
even if their resumes are identical.

00:12:59.184 --> 00:13:02.682
Candidates with foreign accents
are less likely to get called back too,